---
import Page from "../layouts/Page.astro";
import PageHeader from "@oblivios/site-shared/components/PageHeader.astro";
import Print from "@oblivios/site-shared/components/Print.astro";
import { security } from "../lib/records.mjs";
import { securityTxt } from "../lib/securitytxt.mjs";
import { sources, own } from "../lib/site.mjs";

sources("security", ["SECURITY.md", "security-contact.asc", "The contact, the key validity and the fingerprint are read from SECURITY.md when the page is built."]);
const txt = securityTxt();
---
<Page
  title="Security: ObliviOS"
  description="How to report a vulnerability in ObliviOS, the PGP key and fingerprint, and what to expect."
  path="/security"
  current="/security"
>
  <PageHeader crumb="Security" title="Security" lede="How to report a vulnerability in the ObliviOS source, what to expect, and the key to encrypt to.">
    <Print id="k" label="A key" />
  </PageHeader>
  <section class="band">
    <div class="c">
      <div class="prose">
        <h2>Reporting a vulnerability</h2>
        <p>Open an issue, or send an email to <a href={`mailto:${security.email}`}>{security.email}</a>. An issue is public: if you would rather the problem is not public before it is fixed, use the email. Plain text is fine; you can encrypt it with the PGP key below if you want to, but you do not have to.</p>
        <p>Please include what is affected (file, patch or package), how to reproduce the problem, and the impact you expect.</p>
        <h2>The key</h2>
        <div class="keycard">
          <div class="kt">ObliviOS Security</div>
          <div class="ks">ed25519, with a cv25519 encryption subkey · valid until {security.validUntil}</div>
          <div class="kl">Fingerprint</div>
          <div class="fp">{security.fingerprint[0]}<br />{security.fingerprint[1]}</div>
          <p class="kf">Compare this fingerprint with the key before you encrypt to it. The public key is <a href="/security-contact.asc"><code>security-contact.asc</code></a>, in every repository.</p>
        </div>
        <h2>What to expect</h2>
        <ul><li>I reply within 3 days.</li><li>I agree a disclosure date with you. There is no fixed time to a fix.</li><li>I credit you in the fix unless you ask me not to.</li><li>There is no bug bounty.</li></ul>
        <h2>Scope</h2>
        <p>In scope: the patches, services and scripts in the ObliviOS repositories. ObliviOS is source only, so there is no build, image or update service to report on. A weakness that exists in upstream GrapheneOS or AOSP is better reported to those projects. Tell me as well if my patches make it worse.</p>
        <h2>Which sites are mine</h2>
        <p>{own} The contact and the key on this page are the only ones I use for reports.</p>
        <h2><code>security.txt</code></h2>
        <p>The same contact is served as <a href="/.well-known/security.txt"><code>/.well-known/security.txt</code></a> (RFC 9116):</p>
        <pre tabindex="0">{txt}</pre>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Page>
